{
  "summary": "Refactors BIP32 derivation path representations and descriptor parsing so multipath descriptors are stored within a single Descriptor object instead of being expanded into multiple descriptors. Introduces KeyPath and KeyPathElement classes to preserve multipath elements and the original hardening character during parsing. Modifies Parse() to return a single Descriptor pointer, providing GetMultipathExpansion() and IsMultipath() for callers that need the expanded forms.",
  "problem": "Multipath descriptor strings were treated purely as syntactic sugar and discarded during parsing, expanding into a vector of distinct descriptors. Because the parsed descriptor objects lacked the multipath representation, the node could not regenerate or return the original multipath string via RPCs such as getdescriptorinfo.",
  "evidence": [
   "PR description: 'Currently, multipath descriptor strings treat the multipath specifiers as syntactic sugar. Once we finish parsing such a string, the multipath elements are lost... This means that we are unable to return the multipath string for such descriptors.'",
   "test/functional/rpc_getdescriptorinfo.py asserts that getdescriptorinfo returns the original multipath descriptor string instead of the first expanded child descriptor"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36443",
      "#36444"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "A wide-reaching mechanical update replaces std::vector<uint32_t> derivation paths with KeyPath and KeyPathElement across utility, wallet, signing, RPC, and test code, while descriptor parsing internals are refactored to prevent premature expansion.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased onto the latest master branch with no changes to the commit structure or design.",
  "card": "Represents multipath descriptors natively in a single Descriptor object rather than immediately expanding them into multiple descriptors during parsing. Previously, multipath notation was treated as syntactic sugar and discarded upon parsing, preventing RPCs such as getdescriptorinfo from returning or preserving the original multipath string. Derivation path parsing is restructured into KeyPath and KeyPathElement classes to retain multipath branches and hardening styles, while callers requiring individual paths use GetMultipathExpansion. This refactor serves as a prerequisite for follow-up multipath work in #36443 and #36444.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
